@page "/"
@attribute [StaticPage]

<StaticMetadata Title="Blazorade Static Pages" Date="2026-08-24" />

<StaticContent>

    <h1>Blazorade Static Pages</h1>

    <p class="lead">
        Build ordinary Blazor WebAssembly applications and make their important content visible to
        search engines and other crawlers.
    </p>

    <p>
        Blazorade Static Pages adds build-time static page generation without replacing the Blazor
        development model. Your routable components, layouts, navigation, and reusable components
        remain the source of truth for the application.
    </p>

    <h2>How it works</h2>

    <p>
        Mark a routable component with <code>[StaticPage]</code>, then place the content that
        should be available in the generated HTML inside it. At runtime, the marker renders no
        wrapper element, so the application keeps its normal interactive behavior.
    </p>

    <div class="row g-4 my-2">
        <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="card h-100">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h3 class="card-title h5">Application-first</h3>
                    <p class="card-text">
                        Use standard Blazor tooling and components. Static output is generated from
                        the application you already build.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="card h-100">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h3 class="card-title h5">Crawler-visible HTML</h3>
                    <p class="card-text">
                        Important page content is available in the generated HTML before JavaScript
                        runs, improving discoverability and initial delivery.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="card h-100">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h3 class="card-title h5">Interactive by default</h3>
                    <p class="card-text">
                        Static generation does not remove Blazor interactivity. Runtime-only content
                        can be excluded when needed.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Core building blocks</h2>

    <ul>
        <li><strong>StaticPageAttribute</strong> identifies a page for static generation.</li>
        <li><strong>StaticMetadata</strong> defines generated page metadata.</li>
        <li><strong>StaticContent</strong> provides a reusable component's static representation.</li>
        <li><strong>InteractiveContent</strong> marks a subtree that belongs only to the runtime application.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        This page is itself a development sample: it is a regular routable Blazor component using
        <code>StaticPageAttribute</code>, while also providing realistic content for testing the generator.
    </p>
</StaticContent>
